{"parentUuid":"10489cb6-c81f-45c3-8f0d-93891870b686","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Goroa5cYTyZzJSLFXQiTJf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT inprocessing_dtime_ratio parameter SAT preprocessing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter for symmetry finding dtime limit · Issue #4419 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4419\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the `inprocessing_dtime_ratio` parameter in OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver:\n\nThe `inprocessing_dtime_ratio` parameter (optional double, default value 0.2) specifies the proportion at each \"restart\" - if the proportion is below this ratio, the solver will perform inprocessing, otherwise it skips inprocessing for that restart.\n\nThe parameter controls the amount of dtime (decision time) the solver should spend on probing for each inprocessing round.\n\nThis parameter is defined in the OR-Tools SAT solver's `sat_parameters.proto` configuration file and is part of the SAT preprocessing and inprocessing mechanism that helps optimize constraint satisfaction problems by reducing problem complexity during solving.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6fcdfecf-b4b4-4b06-8844-4e192d6ccf67","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:01.880Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"10489cb6-c81f-45c3-8f0d-93891870b686","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6ba72053-c09c-43ed-85de-d161d515e2a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018PzXiHLdD8dFrTGZdi5Nm1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Kissat 4.x inprocessing schedule SAT competition 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/kissat · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - texmex76/kissat-cr\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/texmex76/kissat-cr\"},{\"title\":\"kissat/README.md at master · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"FreshPorts -- math/kissat: Kissat SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.freshports.org/math/kissat/\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/results.html\"},{\"title\":\"PL-PRS-BVA-KISSAT in SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://dl.lre.epita.fr/papers/saoudi.24.pos.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jix/kissat_extras: A fork of the Kissat SAT solver with additional features. Supports incremental solving.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jix/kissat_extras\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about Kissat's participation in the SAT Competition 2024 and 2025:\n\n## Kissat Overview\nKissat is a \"keep it simple and clean bare metal SAT solver\" written in C. It is a port of CaDiCaL back to C with improved data structures, better scheduling of inprocessing and optimized algorithms and implementation.\n\n## SAT Competition Participation\n\n**SAT Competition 2024:**\nYou can get more information about Kissat in the SAT Competition 2024 proceedings by Armin Biere, Tobias Faller, Katalin Fazekas, Mathias Fleury, Nils Froleyks and Florian Pollitt in \"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2024.\"\n\n**SAT Competition 2025:**\nKissat was also described in the Proceedings of SAT Competition 2025: Solver and Benchmark Descriptions, Vienna, 2025.\n\nThe search results confirm Kissat's participation in both competitions, and the official solver descriptions from these competitions (published as PDFs in the results) would contain detailed information about the specific inprocessing schedule implementation, though the full technical details are not excerpted in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e121c949-faa6-4c75-b5d1-3e0847ae9d8c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:02.694Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6ba72053-c09c-43ed-85de-d161d515e2a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"65f7d754-bed9-4aab-9621-22b8670d93e4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018vGmPDCknSBwUWhYVgnUam","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT solver inprocessing techniques 2025 vivification bounded variable elimination\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A New Variable Ordering for In-processing Bounded ...\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-04145361v1/file/A_New_Variable_Ordering_for_In_processing_Bounded_Variable_Elimination_in_SAT_Solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Effective Preprocessing in SAT Through Variable and Clause Elimination\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220944383_Effective_Preprocessing_in_SAT_Through_Variable_and_Clause_Elimination\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/html/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27.html\"},{\"title\":\"Preprocessing in SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereJarvisaloKiesl-SAT-Handbook-2021-Preprocessing-Chapter-Manuscript.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A New Variable Ordering for In-processing Bounded Variable Elimination in SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/373079608_A_New_Variable_Ordering_for_In-processing_Bounded_Variable_Elimination_in_SAT_Solvers\"},{\"title\":\"Integer Linear Programming Preprocessing for Maximum Satisfiability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.06216v3\"},{\"title\":\"Clause vivification by unit propagation in CDCL SAT solvers | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/337041507_Clause_vivification_by_unit_propagation_in_CDCL_SAT_solvers\"},{\"title\":\"A New Variable Ordering for In-processing Bounded Variable Elimination in SAT Solvers - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-04145361\"},{\"title\":\"Effective Preprocessing in SAT Through Variable and Clause Elimination | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/11499107_5\"},{\"title\":\"ILP Techniques for Enhancing Branch and Bound MaxSAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"http://arxiv.org/html/2506.06216v2\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for SAT solver inprocessing techniques, vivification, and bounded variable elimination:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Bounded Variable Elimination (BVE):**\nBounded Variable Elimination (BVE) is an important Boolean formula simplification technique in which the variable ordering is crucial. While other formula simplification techniques such as clause vivification, self-subsuming resolution and equivalence reasoning usually produce a formula smaller and easier to solve, BVE can produce a formula harder to solve.\n\n**Recent Work on Variable Ordering:**\nA new variable ordering ESA for in-processing BVE has been defined. Experimental results on all the 5675 different instances which have been used in the Application, Crafted, and Main tracks of all SAT Competitions up to 2022 show that the new ordering ESA consistently allows the base solvers improvements.\n\n**Clause Vivification:**\nLearnt clauses in CDCL SAT solvers often contain redundant literals, which may have a negative impact on performance because redundant literals may deteriorate both the effectiveness of Boolean constraint propagation and the quality of subsequent learnt clauses. To overcome this drawback, a new inprocessing SAT approach eliminates redundant literals from learnt clauses by applying Boolean constraint propagation.\n\n**Parallel and Distributed Approaches (2025):**\nRecent work from the 2025 SAT competition discusses shared-memory parallelization of certain techniques including subsumption, clause strengthening, and bounded variable elimination (BVE). Additionally, vivification-like inprocessing could be elegantly achieved in a parallel fashion by adding a second pure clause strengthening thread to each CDCL solver.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"15adc830-eba8-4782-9249-fd1535e939c8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:02.973Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"65f7d754-bed9-4aab-9621-22b8670d93e4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8121c6bd-9c93-4512-a5d7-53a2b1e9e410","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DCk7kThwNcrXK6bctWiagL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL 2.x inprocessing techniques list 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 Armin Biere1,2(B) , Tobias Faller1 , Katalin Fazekas3\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24-Springer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing | Formal Methods in System Design | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10703-023-00432-z\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Submitted by Nils Froleyks Submitted at Institute for Formal Models\",\"url\":\"https://froleyks.de/assets/pdf/Deep%20integration%20of%20SAT%20solving%20and%20model%20checking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Proofs for Incremental SAT with Inprocessing Benjamin Kiesl-Reiter\",\"url\":\"https://assets.amazon.science/0f/27/487a4cb24557b9a5d8d4613af264/proofs-for-incremental-sat-with-inprocessing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] CADICAL at the SAT Race 2019 | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/CADICAL-at-the-SAT-Race-2019-Biere/52696d00f528d104aeb02bff12630b985dffe075\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Inprocessing Rules | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/268667939_Inprocessing_Rules\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about CaDiCaL 2.x inprocessing techniques:\n\n## CaDiCaL 2.0 Inprocessing Techniques\n\nThe heart of the solver is the function cdcl_loop_with_inprocessing in Internal which interleaves the CDCL loop with formula simplification steps (i.e., with inprocessing).\n\nDuring Search, CaDiCaL supports several techniques, like chronological backtracking, rephasing, and shrinking.\n\n### Recent Developments (2024-2025)\n\nFor the SAT Competition 2025, the new submitted version of CaDiCaL is available on the development branch on Github, with its code base increased roughly from 46 KLOC to 64 KLOC of C++, needed to support the following techniques ported from Kissat, though the specific techniques are not fully detailed in the search results.\n\nAdditionally, implementation of gate extraction and congruence closure is fast enough to run until completion whenever it is scheduled initially and during inprocessing, and they further added an internal version of bounded variable addition.\n\nThe search results reference the official CaDiCaL 2.0 paper from CAV 2024 which would contain a comprehensive list of inprocessing techniques. For a complete and detailed list of all inprocessing techniques, I recommend consulting the full CAV 2024 paper or the CaDiCaL GitHub repository directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7a81c6a8-3c67-4013-b038-d6a20d60f79c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:03.182Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8121c6bd-9c93-4512-a5d7-53a2b1e9e410","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
