{"parentUuid":"8d8f8f3e-345a-49f9-83c6-60876429ed97","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxwN6FQQkPNyVBuKgNyj1w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT vivification probing SAT sweeping parameters sat_parameters.proto\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about your query:\n\nGoogle's OR-Tools contains documentation and resources for the CP-SAT solver, and the sat_parameters.proto file is located in the OR-Tools repository.\n\nThe CP-SAT solver offers numerous parameters to control its behavior, which are implemented via Protocol Buffers. The well-documented proto file can be found in the official repository, which would be the sat_parameters.proto file you're referencing.\n\nThe search results reference specific SAT solving techniques used in the OR-Tools CP-SAT implementation. You can access the sat_parameters.proto file directly on GitHub at https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto, which contains the comprehensive parameter definitions for controlling SAT solving strategies including vivification, probing, sweeping, and other advanced SAT techniques.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"61e2ddb6-acbe-48a7-aba5-5c7e2bea3971","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:13.950Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d8f8f3e-345a-49f9-83c6-60876429ed97","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"376ebe24-cba4-4a58-b55a-972d84a76b9d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NVo1fLrNLFyDRwu7m4wNUB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT presolve_bve_threshold subsumption blocked clause elimination parameter\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SatPresolver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/simplification/SatPresolver\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Effective Preprocessing in SAT Through Variable and Clause Elimination\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220944383_Effective_Preprocessing_in_SAT_Through_Variable_and_Clause_Elimination\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Preprocessing in SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereJarvisaloKiesl-SAT-Handbook-2021-Preprocessing-Chapter-Manuscript.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Clause Elimination for SAT and QSAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/10942/26071/20415\"},{\"title\":\"Clause elimination for SAT and QSAT | Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/2831071.2831075\"},{\"title\":\"Eﬀective Preprocessing in SAT through Variable and Clause Elimination\",\"url\":\"https://scispace.com/pdf/effective-preprocessing-in-sat-through-variable-and-clause-6rvzraqg1h.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Impact of Bounded Variable Elimination on Solving Pigeonhole Formulas\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~mheule/publications/bve-paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Blocked Clause Elimination Matti J¨arvisalo1, Armin Biere2, and Marijn Heule3\",\"url\":\"https://fmv.jku.at/papers/JarvisaloBiereHeule-TACAS10.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about the `presolve_bve_threshold` parameter in CP-SAT.\n\nDuring presolve, the `presolve_bve_threshold` parameter controls whether CP-SAT will attempt bounded variable elimination (BVE) of a variable x by checking if the number of occurrences of x times the number of occurrences of not(x) is not greater than this parameter.\n\nThe search results also show that this parameter is part of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver, which uses presolving techniques including subsumption, self-subsuming resolution, and variable elimination by clause distribution. Additionally, blocked clauses are one of the most important types of redundant clauses that can be removed during preprocessing, where a clause is blocked if it contains a literal such that all resolvents upon this literal are tautologies.\n\nThese techniques work together in the presolve phase to simplify SAT problems before the solver begins its main search procedure.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fab199b4-3d7d-432d-b5de-5b6e4fda3f55","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:15.847Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"376ebe24-cba4-4a58-b55a-972d84a76b9d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"16fa9dd1-9d40-43f1-a0b6-1a2e47e2d588","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPMzbxuMRCRRM9GdnaEut3","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Solver Inprocessing & Presolve Parameters\n\n## Inprocessing Parameters\n- **use_sat_inprocessing** (default: true) - \"Enable or disable inprocessing which is some SAT presolving done at each restart\"\n- **inprocessing_dtime_ratio** (default: 0.2) - Proportion of deterministic time allocated to inprocessing per restart cycle\n- **inprocessing_probing_dtime** (default: 1.0) - Deterministic time budget for probing during each inprocessing round\n- **inprocessing_minimization_dtime** (default: 1.0) - Time spent on learnt clause minimization techniques per inprocessing phase\n- **inprocessing_minimization_use_conflict_analysis** (default: true) - Apply conflict analysis during minimization\n- **inprocessing_minimization_use_all_orderings** (default: false) - Try all orderings during minimization\n- **inprocessing_use_congruence_closure** (default: true) - Enable clausal congruence closure algorithm\n- **inprocessing_use_sat_sweeping** (default: false) - Enable SAT sweeping algorithm for equivalence detection\n\n## Presolve Parameters\n- **cp_model_presolve** (default: true) - Whether to presolve the constraint programming model\n- **cp_model_probing_level** (default: 2) - Effort level for probing (0 disables completely)\n- **cp_model_use_sat_presolve** (default: true) - Apply SAT presolve alongside CP presolve\n- **presolve_bve_threshold** (default: 500) - Occurrence limit for bounded variable elimination attempts\n- **presolve_bve_clause_weight** (default: 3) - Weight multiplier for clause cost during BVE decisions\n- **presolve_blocked_clause** (default: true) - Detect basic blocked clause cases\n- **presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit** (default: 30.0) - Maximum deterministic time for probing\n- **presolve_use_bva** (default: true) - Enable bounded variable addition during presolve\n- **presolve_bva_threshold** (default: 1) - Minimum clause reduction required for adding variables\n\n## Subsumption & Clause Analysis\n- **subsumption_during_conflict_analysis** (default: true) - \"Detect if some involved reasons are subsumed by current conflict\"\n- **extra_subsumption_during_conflict_analysis** (default: true) - Additional subsumption detection during conflict resolution\n- **decision_subsumption_during_conflict_analysis** (default: true) - Further subsumption options during conflict analysis\n- **eagerly_subsume_last_n_conflicts** (default: 4) - Number of recent learned clauses to check for subsumption\n- **subsume_during_vivification** (default: true) - Remove clauses implied by others during vivification\n\n## Binary Minimization & Conflict Processing\n- **binary_minimization_algorithm** (default: BINARY_MINIMIZATION_FROM_UIP_AND_DECISIONS) - Strategy for using binary clauses to minimize learned clauses\n- **minimization_algorithm** (default: RECURSIVE) - Conflict minimization approach (NONE, SIMPLE, or RECURSIVE)"}]},"uuid":"9bfcdbcb-f03b-46c0-bc44-49d125c1f217","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:19.401Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16fa9dd1-9d40-43f1-a0b6-1a2e47e2d588","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
