{"parentUuid":"c9c3686d-be46-4797-a520-7a716a5c45ec","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b55e8deb-71cd-4096-967c-371d63aeb2d3","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWxMUDaEf8Q37oJKZ1H6Ed","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL Kissat 2025 \"congruence closure\" \"gate extraction\" \"bounded variable addition\" inprocessing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solver Etudes I | Hey There Buddo!\",\"url\":\"https://www.philipzucker.com/python_sat/\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"kissat/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/kissat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"CADICAL, KISSAT, PARACOOBA, PLINGELING and TREENGELING\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/BiereFazekasFleuryHeisinger-SAT-Competition-2020-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Kissat with various options of gates and definitions in variable... | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Kissat-with-various-options-of-gates-and-definitions-in-variable-elimination_fig4_370226372\"},{\"title\":\"Proofs for Incremental SAT with Inprocessing Benjamin Kiesl-Reiter\",\"url\":\"https://assets.amazon.science/0f/27/487a4cb24557b9a5d8d4613af264/proofs-for-incremental-sat-with-inprocessing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/kissat · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CaDiCaL and Kissat for 2025 with the techniques you mentioned:\n\n## SAT Competition 2025 Solvers\n\nSeveral key techniques from Kissat have been ported to CaDiCaL, with the new submitted version available on the development branch on Github. The code base increased from roughly 46 KLOC to 64 KLOC of C++ to support techniques ported from Kissat.\n\n### Key Techniques\n\n**Congruence Closure and Gate Extraction:** The implementation of gate extraction and congruence closure is fast enough to run until completion whenever it is scheduled initially and during inprocessing.\n\n**Bounded Variable Addition:** An internal version of bounded variable addition was further added.\n\n### Additional Context\n\nKissat dominated the main track of the SAT Competition 2024 with 3 gold medals, using core techniques including congruence closure (SAT'24), clausal equivalence sweeping (FMCAD'24), bounded variable addition (BVA) and vivification.\n\nThe search results reference the official solver descriptions for SAT Competition 2025, which provide detailed information about how these techniques are integrated into both CaDiCaL and Kissat solvers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ca4334de-c9c3-48e1-919f-5c3be03ddd48","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:49.957Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c9c3686d-be46-4797-a520-7a716a5c45ec","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"706625e3-2977-4f33-b7b7-4111662cd7b8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b55e8deb-71cd-4096-967c-371d63aeb2d3","agentId":"aa365953ef6c4d7eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNoBQ8uBHRq9mgnV5Asgic","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Solver Parameters: Presolve and Inprocessing\n\n## Presolve Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `presolve_bve_threshold` | int32 | 500 | Bounded variable elimination (BVE) threshold for occurrence count |\n| `filter_sat_postsolve_clauses` | bool | false | Optimization flag for postsolve clause filtering in BVE |\n| `presolve_bve_clause_weight` | int32 | 3 | Weight multiplier for clause count during BVE |\n| `presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit` | double | 30.0 | Deterministic time limit for probing in SAT presolve |\n| `presolve_blocked_clause` | bool | true | Enables heuristic detection of blocked clauses |\n| `presolve_use_bva` | bool | true | Enables Bounded Variable Addition (BVA) |\n| `presolve_bva_threshold` | int32 | 1 | Minimum clause reduction required to apply BVA |\n| `max_presolve_iterations` | int32 | 3 | Maximum presolve iterations for large reductions |\n| `cp_model_presolve` | bool | true | Enables presolve on constraint programming models |\n| `cp_model_use_sat_presolve` | bool | true | Uses SAT presolve alongside CP presolve |\n| `load_at_most_ones_in_sat_presolve` | bool | false | Loads at-most-one constraints in SAT presolve |\n| `remove_fixed_variables_early` | bool | true | Remaps fixed variables before full presolve |\n| `presolve_substitution_level` | int32 | 1 | Controls variable substitution/aggregation effort |\n| `presolve_extract_integer_enforcement` | bool | false | Extracts enforcement literals from linear constraints |\n| `presolve_inclusion_work_limit` | int64 | 100000000 | Work limit for subsumption detection operations |\n| `infer_all_diffs` | bool | true | Detects all-different constraints via max-clique |\n| `find_big_linear_overlap` | bool | true | Finds and merges large overlapping linear expressions |\n| `find_clauses_that_are_exactly_one` | bool | true | Promotes clauses to exactly-one constraints |\n\n## Inprocessing Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `use_sat_inprocessing` | bool | true | Enables SAT presolving at each restart to root level |\n| `inprocessing_dtime_ratio` | double | 0.2 | Proportion of deterministic time spent on inprocessing |\n| `inprocessing_probing_dtime` | double | 1.0 | Deterministic time for probing per inprocessing round |\n| `inprocessing_minimization_dtime` | double | 1.0 | Time for clause minimization during inprocessing |\n| `inprocessing_minimization_use_conflict_analysis` | bool | true | Uses conflict analysis for clause minimization |\n| `inprocessing_minimization_use_all_orderings` | bool | false | Tests all variable orderings for minimization |\n| `inprocessing_use_congruence_closure` | bool | true | Enables clausal congruence closure algorithm |\n| `inprocessing_use_sat_sweeping` | bool | false | Enables SAT sweeping algorithm for clause equivalence |\n\n## Subsumption Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `subsumption_during_conflict_analysis` | bool | true | Detects subsumed clauses during 1-UIP conflict computation |\n| `extra_subsumption_during_conflict_analysis` | bool | true | Additional subsumption from intermediate conflict clauses |\n| `decision_subsumption_during_conflict_analysis` | bool | true | Further subsumption options during conflict analysis |\n| `eagerly_subsume_last_n_conflicts` | int32 | 4 | Subsumes last N learned clauses with new conflicts |\n| `subsume_during_vivification` | bool | true | Removes clauses implied by vivification process |\n\n## Probing Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `probing_deterministic_time_limit` | double | 1.0 | Time limit for probing in CP-SAT presolve |\n| `use_probing_search` | bool | false | Enables continuous variable and bound probing during search |\n| `use_extended_probing` | bool | true | Extends probing to bool_or and cardinality constraints |\n| `probing_num_combinations_limit` | int32 | 20000 | Variable pair/triplet combinations to scan in probing |"}]},"uuid":"298c54fe-2ca3-4ded-9ae3-16120f22c8ff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:58.485Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"706625e3-2977-4f33-b7b7-4111662cd7b8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
